{"name":"Glowing Lantern","hex":"#fbb736","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"glowing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of glow"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The action of glowing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glowing"},{"term":"lantern","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A case of translucent or transparent material made to protect a flame, or light, used to illuminate its surroundings.","Especially, a metal casing with lens used to illuminate a stage (e.g. spotlight, floodlight)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To furnish with a lantern."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lantern"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lantern","blocks":[{"text":"A lantern is a source of lighting, often portable. It typically features a protective enclosure for the light source – historically usually a candle, a wick in oil, or a heated mesh, and often a battery-powered light in modern times – to make it easier to carry and hang up, and make it more reliable outdoors or in drafty interiors. Lanterns may also be used for signaling, as torches, or as general light-sources outdoors."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/CNW_brakeman%27s_kerosene_lantern.JPG/330px-CNW_brakeman%27s_kerosene_lantern.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lantern","wikidata":"Q862454"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/CNW_brakeman%27s_kerosene_lantern.JPG/330px-CNW_brakeman%27s_kerosene_lantern.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/CNW_brakeman%27s_kerosene_lantern.JPG/330px-CNW_brakeman%27s_kerosene_lantern.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A railroad brakeman's signal lantern, fueled by kerosene.","link":"h